## 1. Leap's measurements, fitted [K -> P]
  NAX4 ms per layer = 0.094 + 10.15 us x groups  (8 points, residual rms 4 us; distinct experts do not enter)
  3c   ms per layer = 0.042 + 7.08 us x (row, rank) pairs  (residual rms 10 us; groups do not enter)
  per-group MMA floor at the probe's peak (K-62e: 0.60 ms / 82 groups): 7.32 us  = 9,600 ops of 16 x 32 x 16 at 1.3 G op/s = 7.38 us
  bytes per group (k62p layer 20 S 16: 143 MB / 72.4 groups): 1.98 MB -> 7.66 us at 258 GB/s, 6.95 us at 284 GB/s, 6.72 us at 294 GB/s; per distinct expert 2.37 MB
  measured per group (the fit): 10.2 us = MMA floor x 1.39; the fixed 0.094 ms per call = 1.3 us per group at 72 groups
  85 % of streaming at 284 GB/s allows 8.18 us per group all-in; the MMA floor alone is 7.32 us (0.89 x the budget): structurally over it at the probe's peak
  K-62e's zero-DRAM run (codes from one row): 0.70 of 0.85-0.90 ms -> exposed DRAM ~2.1 us per group; A-operand marshalling ~25 % of the MMA time (nax_tput mode 2) ~1.8 us

