## 5. Order sensitivity of one tensor op's 32-term sum (bf16 x times uint4 code, fp32) on real activations [K numeric]
  chunks where the fp32 result depends on the order: 0.00 % of 81920; chunks whose exact sum is not an fp32 number: 0.00 %
  -> an ALU path can match the tensor op bit for bit only where the exact sum is fp32-representable AND the op rounds once; the op's internal order is not public, so the hybrid is not certifiable as bitwise

